course: dictionary
lesson: 14726
title: Profound: very great and very deep
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Profound is a word you will meet in stories, science and big questions. It can mean very great or very strong. «The news brought a profound sadness to the whole village.» The sadness is very strong, so profound means very great.
explain: Profound can also describe deep thinking. «Her question was profound: why do we dream?» A profound question makes you think hard about something important. Ask yourself: is this very big, very strong, or very deep? The words around the hard word will tell you which.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The music had a profound effect on everyone» still makes sense with very strong in place of profound, so very strong is the right meaning here.
fact: Profound means very great or very strong.
fact: Profound also means showing deep thinking and understanding.
fact: «A profound silence» means a very deep, complete silence.
fact: In medicine, profound deafness means being almost completely deaf.
fact: Profound is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a profound effect» or «a profound question».
exercise: «The music had a profound effect on everyone in the hall.» What does profound mean here? | Very late | Very cold | Very small | *Very strong
exercise: «Her answer showed profound understanding of the poem.» What does profound suggest? | *Deep thinking and understanding | Sleepy and tired | Careless guessing | Loud and cheerful
exercise: Which word could replace profound in «a profound effect» without changing the meaning much? | late | *great | dull | tiny
test: «The news caused a profound change in how we farm.» Which meaning fits best? | *A very big change | A change in the weather | A change that was never noticed | A tiny change
test: «Grandma asked a profound question about life.» What kind of question is it? | A question with a very short answer | A question about the time | A question asked too loudly | *A question that makes you think deeply
exam: What does «profound deafness» mean? | Being able to hear very loud music | Wearing ear protectors all day | Hearing a little better than before | *Being almost completely deaf
